Add cargo-fuzz targets `blean` and `ndjson` (upstream has none)

Both import the input with import::import_bytes and check every own
declaration with the value core, as nl-fast does by default (fresh session
after a failure or past 16 MiB). `blean` takes inputs with the blean magic,
`ndjson` all others. Budgets are cut from nl-fast's 200M steps / 4 GiB per
declaration to 1M steps / 64 MiB.
Upstream: none (no fuzz targets or fuzzing issues, checked 2026-11-22).

